    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). There's a single data-driven `AcceptanceTest` class, and the run log confirms the new duplicate-email scenario was exercised (`Duplicate owner email at POST /api/owners: owner5@example.test` \u2192 409) and passed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the lower-cased email is already used by another owner, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException` pattern:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException`** (new) \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/advice/DuplicateEmailException.java`, a runtime exception carrying the rejected (lower-cased) email.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added `handleDuplicateEmailException`, mapping it to `409 CONFLICT` with an `errors: [\"email\"]` body, matching the other duplicate handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the email, calls the new `rejectDuplicateEmail(email)` before saving. The helper skips the check when no email was supplied (email is optional) and compares against existing owners' emails case-insensitively, throwing `DuplicateEmailException` on a match.\n\nEmails are already normalized to lower-case on store, and the comparison uses `equalsIgnoreCase` for safety against any legacy mixed-case data.",
